    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51452" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vulturnus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Volt-</span></b> ), i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river in
			Campania</i>, the mod. <i>Volturno</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
			11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7, 729 al.</span></i>—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vulturnus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Volt-</span></b> ), a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Vulturnus</i>, <i>Vulturnian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vada,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					12, 521</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amnis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					36, 26, 66, § 194</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oppidum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 3,
					5, 9, § 61</span></i>
			.</div>
